---
import LegalDocument from "../../components/legal/LegalDocument.astro";

const sections = [
  {
    title: "General principle",
    paragraphs: [
      "LKProfessionals provides professional and custom technology services. Payments commonly cover reserved project capacity, analysis, design, development, configuration, licences, hosting, domains or other work already performed or committed.",
      "For that reason, payments are not automatically refundable simply because a client later decides not to continue.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Advance and milestone payments",
    paragraphs: [
      "Advance, deposit and milestone payments may become non-refundable once the associated work has started, resources have been committed or third-party costs have been incurred.",
      "The specific quotation or agreement for a project takes precedence where it contains its own cancellation or refund terms.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Third-party costs",
    paragraphs: [
      "Charges paid or committed for domains, hosting, software licences, advertising, external services, transaction fees or other third-party products are generally subject to the refund rules of the relevant provider.",
      "LKProfessionals cannot guarantee recovery of third-party costs already incurred on behalf of a client.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Cancellation before work begins",
    paragraphs: [
      "Where a client cancels before substantive work has started and before non-recoverable third-party costs have been incurred, LKProfessionals may review whether part or all of the relevant payment can reasonably be refunded.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Completed or delivered work",
    paragraphs: [
      "Fees relating to work already completed, demonstrated, delivered or made available are generally not refundable.",
      "If there is a genuine issue with agreed deliverables, the normal first step is to allow reasonable opportunity for correction within the agreed project scope.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Refund requests",
    paragraphs: [
      "Refund requests should be submitted in writing with the relevant project, invoice or payment details and the reason for the request.",
      "Requests may be sent to info@lkprofessionals.com and will be reviewed against the project scope, work completed, costs incurred and any project-specific agreement.",
    ],
  },
];
---

<LegalDocument
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How LKProfessionals handles project deposits, completed work, cancellations and eligible refund requests."
  canonicalPath="/legal/refund-policy/"
  updated="14 August 2026"
  sections={sections}
/>
